## Trade-offs Accepted

| Trade-off | What we gave up | Why it's acceptable |
|-----------|----------------|---------------------|
| Shared DB multi-tenancy | Full data isolation between orgs | Acceptable for B2B SaaS; can migrate to separate schemas if compliance requires it |
| At-least-once job delivery | Guaranteed exactly-once execution | All handlers are idempotent; simpler than distributed transactions |
| JWT (not session cookies) | Stateless is harder to invalidate immediately | JTI blocklist in Redis closes the gap; 15-min TTL limits window |
| Monorepo | Independent deploy cadence per service | Not needed at current team size; revisit at 5+ services |
| No E2E encryption for stored data | Data at rest readable by server operators | Acceptable for B2B; customer-managed encryption is a roadmap item |
